#!/usr/bin/env node
// faff — the bundled CLI for the faff skill suite.
//
// Subcommands:
//   config <path|get|spec-docs-path|dump|resolved> ...  resolve / read .faffrc (resolved = echo non-default slots)
//   config init --set k=v [--set ...] [--force] [--dry-run]   write/merge a tracking block into .faffrc.yaml; --selftest
//   runcheck [--hook] [--recover] [--json] [--selftest] [RUN_DIR]   audit a /faff-beep-boop run ledger; --hook applies the ownership+liveness gate — silent for a foreign HELD run (FAFF-205, heartbeat-only liveness FAFF-233), and a foreign not-held run only WARNs, never hard-blocks (FAFF-235); only an OWNING session or --recover (deliberate human recovery) hard-blocks; --selftest runs the gate table
//   prepcheck [--hook] [--json] [--root DIR]      audit faff-prep attach-state markers; --selftest (FAFF-178)
//   prepcheck --issue ISSUE [--run-dir DIR] [--json] [--root DIR]   FAFF-258: single-issue five-state verdict {attached,parked,open,missing,malformed} (exit 0/0/1/2/2) — reads ONLY .faff/prep/<ISSUE>.json (no global scan); the orchestrator↔prep delegation reconciliation primitive; --json payload carries {issue,state,spec_produced,attached,disposition,owner,ts,owner_matches_run}
//   sentrycheck --hook [--root DIR] [--selftest]   FAFF-471: ADR-0065's cheap ASSIST watchdog locus — a Stop-hook staleness consult, sibling of the runcheck/prepcheck family. Reuses runcheck's ownership/liveness gate (runIsOwned/runIsHeld) verbatim; on EXACTLY the foreign+running+not-held (abandoned-looking) case, spawns one unmodified `faff sentry check --json` child and surfaces a tripped verdict as a non-blocking stderr [warn] naming the remedy commands. Owned / held / not-running / no-run / unreadable-ledger all fast-path to silent exit 0 with no child spawned. Advisory-only at every level — never calls `sentry abort`, never writes the ledger, never exits non-zero or emits a stdout decision payload; --selftest runs the pure gate + consult-classifier table
//   contain <mandate> (--parent <id> | --root) --ancestry <json> [--record <run-id>] [--phase run|tidy|prep|build] [--json]   FAFF-219: subtree-of-mandate containment primitive — walk the agent-supplied parentId chain from <parent> up to <mandate>; contained (exit 0) / outward (exit 3, fail-closed on --root/unknown/cycle/out-of-subtree) / usage (exit 2); PURE (no tracker call); v1 issue-level mandates only. FAFF-354: --ancestry is agent-sourced (binds structure, not truthfulness) — --record appends a containment-check event binding this verdict to the exact ancestry walked (a missing run dir exits 2, before any verdict), so `faff audit` can recompute-and-compare post-hoc (detective, never preventive); --phase (default run) requires --record; --selftest
//   hooks-ensure [--root DIR] [--json] [--dry-run]   idempotently register faff's Stop-hook set (runcheck + prepcheck + sentrycheck) + the PreToolUse merge-fence + background-fence in .claude/settings.json; --selftest (FAFF-192/434/471/491)
//   merge-fence --hook [--root DIR]                FAFF-434: PreToolUse fence — denies a raw gh pr merge Bash call, naming faff merge-gate as the remedy; --hook reads the event on stdin (malformed/absent → exit 0, never block); --selftest runs the matcher table. FAFF-526: ALSO denies a raw base-branch mutation (git merge <feature> on base / git update-ref refs/heads/<base> / git push . HEAD:<base>) — ONLY when the repo has no git remote — naming faff merge-gate --local as the remedy; never blocks base-branch consumption (git merge <base> from a feature branch), and is a no-op on any remote-backed repo
//   background-fence --hook [--root DIR]           FAFF-491: PreToolUse fence — denies a Bash call whose command matches a gate/test-family shape (node --test, faff gates run, npm test, …) AND run_in_background is the strict boolean true, naming the foreground remedy; --hook reads the event on stdin (malformed/absent/non-gate/foreground → exit 0, never block); --selftest runs the matcher table
//   validate-adapters [--skills-dir DIR]          lint shipped slot-skill conformance
//   validate-adapters --configured [--root DIR]   pre-flight a user's configured (swapped-in) slot occupants
//   labels [--names]                              print the canonical faff control-label manifest
//   label add|remove <issue-id> <label> [--present-label L ...]   FAFF-187: emit a faff-contract:label-op descriptor for a control-label mutation (pure, no tracker I/O); --selftest
//   eligible --label L [--label L ...] [--default opt-in|opt-out]   FAFF-61: automation-eligible? (true/false); --selftest
//   next --status S --spec ... [--not-eligible|--parked|--blocked|--if-eligible]   legal next step (JSON); --selftest (--held: alias; --if-eligible: advisory hypothetical)
//   state <issue> [--json] [--root DIR]           local read-model: resolve an issue's local state as JSON (no MCP)
//   queue-state new-key                            print a freshly-minted gitkey (gk-YYYYMMDD-<6xbase36>); pure
//   queue-state derive [--run-dir DIR] [--root DIR] [--json]   FAFF-556: git-only queue_empty/all_parked derivation — diff item-keys (.faff/intake gitkey markers + .faff/specs/*.md filename stems) against a run-ledger's outcomes by exact match; --selftest
//   park-history --now <ISO> [--issue ID] [--root DIR]   deterministic repeat-park counts over .faff/runs summaries (>=3 same root-cause class in 21d); --selftest
//   gitignore-ensure [--root DIR] [--json] [--selftest]   idempotently add faff's local artifacts to .gitignore (overlay matched by the .faffrc.*.yaml glob, FAFF-548); --selftest runs the pattern-set + append-order + idempotency table
//   worktree-prune [--own P ...] [--branch B] [--issue ID] [--dry-run] [--json]   FAFF-126: scoped fail-safe prune — own dangling worktrees only, never repo-wide; --selftest
//   worktree-root [--assert PATH] [--root DIR] [--json]   FAFF-382: single canonical worktree-root resolver + strictly-under assert (env→config→default); --selftest
//   gates <discover|run> [--json]                FAFF-11: cost-ordered engineering-quality gate ladder — discover/run the repo's own declared cheap checks (pre-commit/pkg/Makefile) cheapest-first, fail-fast, emit a faff-contract:quality-gates block; --selftest
//   stage-guard --worktree <dir> --mode assert|filter [--json]   FAFF-457: build-safety staging guard — a filename-class secret check over the index (assert: exit 1 on a staged secret-class path; filter: unstage + report, exit 0). PURE git-plumbing; --selftest
//   corrective-integrity [--consumer corrective|detection|merge-floor] [--run-dir DIR] [--issue ID] [--json]   FAFF-373 (fail-safe) + FAFF-325 (activation): probe asserted:true ONLY from a well-formed FAFF_INTEGRITY_BOUNDARY declaration in pid-1 environ whose dir set covers the required dirs; gate degrades corrective→channel-D / detection→reconcile-only / merge-floor→refuse|unasserted. No crypto; exit 0 (report/degrade, never a hard refuse) / 2 (unknown --consumer); --selftest
//   governance-check --run-dir DIR [--run-dir DIR ...] [--issue ID] [--level L1|L2|L3|L4] [--json] [--summary-md FILE]   FAFF-363: the harness-independent enforcement binding a `.github/actions/governance-check` required status check runs — composes runcheck's completeness audit + the ledger's LAST recorded budget-checkpoint event (never a live token recompute) + merge-gate's floor-artifact re-validation (readAcComplete/readReviewVerdict/readHoldout, never a forked rule) + audit's events↔ledger coherence join, adding no new invariant. Gating legs: completeness, budget (breached at outcome escalate), merge_floor (per target issue: ac-checklist.json + review-verdict.json, + holdout at L4), well-formed owner block; coherence + liveness status/heartbeat-age are REPORT-only. Issue derivation: explicit --issue > branch-name match > every admitted issue with a terminal outcome. Pure evaluator: no network, reads only the given run dirs + repo files; a malformed run-ledger.json is fail-loud exit 2, never a leg failure. exit 0 pass / 1 fail / 2 usage or malformed; --summary-md FILE renders the same job-summary table locally and in CI; --selftest runs the leg + aggregation table
//
// Single public entrypoint. Extensionless executable run directly via its shebang
// (`~/.claude/skills/faff/bin/faff <subcommand>`); `node …/bin/faff <subcommand>` also works.
// Plain CommonJS — no package.json, no dependencies, no install: one thin entrypoint (bin/faff) plus modules under bin/lib/.

// Module layout (FAFF-441): this entrypoint holds only the dispatch shell — USAGE, the
// COMMANDS registry, and main(). Every subcommand's implementation lives in a sibling
// module under bin/lib/, required eagerly below. Modules resolve relative to this file
// (bin/lib/shared-infra.js owns the HERE / ENTRYPOINT path anchors), so both install
// shapes (symlink and CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT copy) work unchanged.
