// ===========================================================================
// === region:shell — dispatch ===
// ===========================================================================
const USAGE = `faff — the bundled CLI for the faff skill suite.

Subcommands:
  config <path|get|spec-docs-path|dump|resolved> ...  resolve / read config (FAFF-387: .faffrc.local.yaml overlay deep-merged over .faffrc.yaml base over DEFAULTS; path is multi-line base-first; resolved echoes both files + non-default slots)
  config init --set k=v [--set ...] [--force] [--dry-run]   write/merge a tracking block into .faffrc.yaml (--selftest runs the table)
  config check [--json] [--root DIR]            FAFF-387: deterministic, read-only posture + integrity checker (NO tracker/network/writes) — parse (base+overlay), git posture (base tracked? overlay ignored?), secret scan (redacted: key-path + length + 4-char prefix, NEVER the value), legacy filename. Exit 0 clean / 1 >=1 finding / 2 unreadable; not-a-git-repo skips posture (reported), parse/secret still run; --selftest runs the secret-pattern + merge + posture tables
  runcheck [--hook] [--recover] [--json] [--selftest] [RUN_DIR]   audit a /faff-beep-boop run ledger; --hook applies the ownership+liveness gate — silent for a foreign HELD run (FAFF-205, heartbeat-only liveness FAFF-233), and a foreign not-held run only WARNs, never hard-blocks (FAFF-235); only an OWNING session or --recover (deliberate human recovery) hard-blocks; --selftest runs the gate table
  heartbeat [RUN_DIR] [--unit ISSUE] [--json]   FAFF-355: the single sanctioned write path for run liveness — refresh the dedicated .faff/runs/<run-id>/heartbeat file to now on the resolved run (arg → $FAFF_RUN_DIR → latest under .faff/runs), so a live-but-quiet build's long sub-steps (faff-graft gate ladder / review / holdout) keep the run HELD instead of ageing out the staleness window (FAFF-205 liveness, heartbeat-only FAFF-233). The tick's ONLY write is that file (tmp + rename) — it never touches the run ledger, so N concurrent tickers can never clobber an orchestrator outcome write. Every read seam overlays the file over the legacy owner.last_heartbeat ledger field (effective heartbeat = the max of both), so a pre-upgrade run keeps working with zero migration. Soft no-op (exit 0, written:false) when there is no ledger / no owner / owner.status != "running" (a done run is never resurrected, and no file is written); exit 2 on a malformed ledger (loud); --json prints { run_dir, last_heartbeat, written, unit }; --selftest runs the effectiveHeartbeatIso/overlayHeartbeat + held-interaction table. FAFF-327: --unit <issue> is the fleet member tick — writes BOTH the run file above AND a dedicated heartbeat.<issue> file (same atomic single-value shape, single-writer by construction — only that member ticks its own file); \`faff sentry check\` reads the member file to resolve member-scoped liveness. An invalid --unit value (empty/traversal-shaped) exits 2 before any write.
  prepcheck [--hook] [--json] [--root DIR]      FAFF-178: audit faff-prep attach-state markers (.faff/prep/*.json) — block on any produced-but-not-attached spec; --hook blocks at Stop (decision payload, exit 0), plain prints a report + exit 3 if open; --selftest runs the table
  prepcheck --issue ISSUE [--run-dir DIR] [--json] [--root DIR]   FAFF-258: single-issue verdict — reads ONLY .faff/prep/<ISSUE>.json (no global scan, additive to --hook which is unchanged), the orchestrator↔prep delegation reconciliation primitive that extends the FAFF-178 same-turn-attach guard to the delegated/autonomous prep boundary. Five-state verdict {attached,parked,open,missing,malformed} — exit 0/0/1/2/2 respectively (attached = spec_produced && attached==true; parked = disposition=="parked", a by-design non-attach; open = produced-but-not-attached with no park disposition, the FAFF-258 drop; missing = no marker file, or spec_produced not true; malformed = unparseable JSON or missing the spec_produced key). --json payload: {issue,state,spec_produced,attached,disposition,owner,ts,owner_matches_run} — owner_matches_run is null unless BOTH --run-dir and the marker's owner.run_dir are present, else the boolean equality. PURE (no tracker call — the orchestrator reconciles against the tracker itself). --selftest runs the five-state table
  sentrycheck --hook [--root DIR] [--selftest]   FAFF-471: ADR-0065's cheap ASSIST watchdog locus, third member of the Stop-hook family alongside runcheck/prepcheck — a staleness-triggered \`faff sentry check\` consult with ZERO new detection math. Reuses runcheck's ownership/liveness gate VERBATIM (runIsOwned/runIsHeld, heartbeat-only per FAFF-233) after overlaying the dedicated heartbeat file (FAFF-355); consults ONLY on the exact foreign+running+not-held (abandoned-looking) case — owned, held, not-running (done/aborted-resumable/legacy no-owner), no run dir, and an unreadable ledger all fast-path to silent exit 0 with NO child spawned (a per-turn-end child on every session would be unacceptable hot-path cost). On consult: spawns exactly one \`faff sentry check --json --run-dir <dir>\` child (bounded at a 10s timeout, mirroring sentryReadBudget's pattern); \`tripped:false\` stays silent (sentry is authoritative); \`tripped:true\` writes ONE non-blocking stderr [warn] line naming the run id, the tripped signal(s), the intervention, and both remedy commands (\`faff sentry check\`/\`faff sentry abort\`); a consult failure (timeout, spawn error, unparseable stdout, or a clean exit-3 indeterminate reply) writes a distinct non-blocking notice ("not an all-clear") rather than swallowing the fault (FAFF-425 posture, softened to advisory because FAFF-235 outranks it at a foreign session's turn-end). Advisory-only at EVERY level, including L4 — the module contains no call to \`sentry abort\` and performs no ledger write; \`--hook\` mode ALWAYS exits 0 and NEVER emits a stdout decision payload (FAFF-235: a foreign run's state must never make an unrelated session un-exitable). --selftest runs the pure gate table (owned via both ownership signals / held / stale-running / done / aborted-resumable / legacy no-owner / unparseable heartbeat / env-override staleness window) plus the consult-outcome classifier table
  intakecheck <issue> [--labels csv] [--interactive] [--json] [--root DIR]   FAFF-212/223: intake-provenance guard — verify a ticket entered through a sanctioned front door (CLI-written .faff/provenance/<ISSUE>.json marker; the spoofable faff-jot-intake label is a grandfather bridge; a human-set faff-automate is admitted as the eligibility-gesture basis — write-abstained ⇒ human-set by construction, FAFF-218); PURE (no tracker call — labels passed via --labels); exit 0 satisfied · 3 unsatisfied under intake_gate=block ONLY (warn never blocks, off always 0) · 2 usage; --interactive makes a block-mode miss exit 0 with a [warn] (human-at-keyboard is the sanction — autonomous OMITS it); malformed marker → absent + warn, never crash; --selftest runs the bases + bypass table. NOT a Stop-hook (would reintroduce FAFF-205)
  intake-record <issue> --via jot|backfill|fast-track [--reason "<text>"] [--initiated interactive|autonomous] [--json] [--root DIR]   FAFF-212/220: write/update the provenance marker (schema 2) and emit a faff-contract:intake-record descriptor (jot Step 4 calls --via jot). MIGRATION / agent-orchestrator tool — NOT the human steady-state remedy (a human just sets faff-automate in the tracker, FAFF-223): --via backfill is for bulk legacy backfill, --via fast-track REQUIRES --reason (recorded override) or exits 2 writing nothing; --initiated stamps the audit-only initiation mode (invalid → exit 2; absent → key omitted, merge-preserved); --selftest runs the via + initiated tables
  contain <mandate> (--parent <id> | --root) --ancestry <json> [--record <run-id>] [--phase run|tidy|prep|build] [--json]   FAFF-219 (Split A of FAFF-217), generalized to container mandates by FAFF-222: subtree-of-mandate containment primitive — answers \`parent ∈ subtree(mandate)\` by walking the AGENT-SUPPLIED ancestry chain (--ancestry, a JSON array of {id, type?, parentId?, projectId?, initiativeId?}) from <parent> up to <mandate>; reaching the mandate = contained, exhausting to a different root / unknown link / cycle = outward. PURE (no tracker call — parity with eligible/next/intakecheck). exit 0 contained · 3 outward (FAIL-CLOSED: --root, unknown/absent link, cycle, or out-of-subtree) · 2 usage/malformed-args. Base case mandate==parent → contained. FAFF-354: --ancestry is agent-sourced, so the walk binds STRUCTURE not truthfulness — --record <run-id> [--phase p] appends a containment-check event binding this verdict to the exact ancestry walked (a missing/non-dir run dir under --record exits 2, BEFORE any verdict — never a silently-unrecorded verdict), so \`faff audit\` can recompute-and-compare post-hoc: a DETECTIVE control, never preventive. Without --record, behaviour is byte-identical. --selftest runs the contained/outward/fail-closed table + the --record run-id traversal-guard table
  budget check [--run-dir DIR] [--until HH:MM] [--max N] [--now-ms MS | --now ISO] [--json]   FAFF-36: run cost / compute budgeting — emit a BudgetState JSON {spent,tokens_source,breached,outcome,warnings?} from the run-ledger + config budget: block + the run's local transcripts. PURE (no tracker/network — parity with next/eligible): tokens summed from the $CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID transcript + child agent-*.jsonl whose own sessionId == this run's (mtime is a cheap pre-filter only, NOT the attribution gate — FAFF-229), baselined at run start; estimate fallback (attempts x est) when the transcript is unavailable, labelled tokens_source=estimate. Dimensions until·max_attempts·tokens·cost (unset = unbounded); at_ceiling stop|narrow|escalate (default stop). --until/--max override config. FAFF-427: budget.cost prices per-model x per-class from a built-in map, unconditionally (pricing:"map" — an unpriced model is priced at the map's costliest known rate, never silently undercounted). FAFF-446: budget.price_per_mtok is REMOVED — a config that still sets it is ignored (named in a warning, never a hard exit) and only a legacy ledger minted before the removal can still carry pricing:"flat" (byte-for-byte, via envelopeFromLedger). Cost warnings surface only when budget.cost is actually configured. A malformed budget.until/--until (not valid HH:MM) never becomes a vacuous ceiling that silently never breaches — it degrades to warnings (present only when non-empty, mirrored to stderr) naming the raw value, breached never contains "until" for it, and exit stays 0 (FAFF-364: a non-zero exit here would fail-OPEN the whole budget signal for sentryReadBudget/run-done --budget, which degrade any non-zero child to the unbreached default). --now-ms <epoch-ms> / --now <ISO> is a HERMETIC test/diagnostic-only clock override for the time-based fields (spent.elapsed_ms + the resolved --until wall) — explicit flag only (no ambient/env form), precedence --now-ms > --now > Date.now() (the production default; no production caller passes it); an unparseable injected value exits 2 (never a silent fall-through) (FAFF-302). breached != {} is the terminating signal. FAFF-425: the run's OWN ledger being unreadable (explicitly-named and absent, or present-but-corrupt) is a distinct own-fault — never coerced into an all-clear reading — emitting {outcome:"indeterminate",indeterminate:true,reason} and exiting 3; a legitimately empty surface (no run requested, none found) is unaffected, unchanged outcome:"none" at exit 0. --selftest runs the table
  economics [--run-dir DIR] [--by class|model|mcp|day|effort] [--json]   FAFF-357: per-run unit economics — emit a UnitEconomics JSON {run_id,tokens_total,tokens_source,price_per_mtok,pricing,cost_total,buckets,shipped_count,attempt_count,cost_per_shipped,cost_per_attempt,per_issue,zero_ship,warnings} deriving cost-per-shipped-issue + cost-per-attempt from the run-ledger outcomes + budget check's transcript-summed this-run tokens. PURE, RENDERING-ONLY (no tracker/network/LLM — parity with budget check/runcheck): reuses budget's exact token path (measureTokens baselined at run start; estimate fallback labelled tokens_source=estimate) and DOES NOT touch any producer (ledger/budget/events unchanged). FAFF-427: the top-line prices via the SAME map + rate source budget.cost uses — pricing:"map", unconditionally, on a fresh resolve; cost_total is THIS RUN's per-model spend (baselined at run start, consistent with tokens_total + budget check's spent.cost), so the "two cost figures" gap (a rate difference, not a population one) is closed — at a run-start baseline of 0 it equals the sum of --by model's priced rows. FAFF-446: budget.price_per_mtok is REMOVED — a fresh config that still sets it is ignored and named in a warning; only a legacy ledger minted before the removal can still carry pricing:"flat", the legacy flat-scalar top-line byte-for-byte; an unpriced model's tokens are excluded from cost_total (reported cost:null for that row, named in warnings) while priced models still sum. cost_* null + no dollar column when nothing could be priced; zero_ship (0 shipped, >0 tokens) flagged loud; attempt_count excludes routed-out/unreached-budget; per_issue is best-effort meta.json attribution (session-owned agent-*.jsonl, [A-Z]+-\d+ in description matched to a ledger outcome), run-level figures never depend on it. beep-boop's Reporting step renders the block. FAFF-410: --by class|model|mcp|day pivots the SAME transcript walk into per-class/per-model/per-day/per-MCP-tool buckets priced per-model×per-class (built-in PRICE_PER_MTOK + optional budget.price_per_mtok_by_model override; unknown model→cost:null); class/model/day reconcile to the top-line total, --by mcp reuses FAFF-409's MEASURED per-tool cache-read attribution; --by X --json rides a breakdown object, --by X (no --json) prints a skimmable table, NO --by is byte-for-byte unchanged; unknown axis exits 2 naming {class,model,mcp,day,effort}; non-leak (sizes/counts/names/model-ids/costs only). FAFF-415: --by effort reads the run's events.jsonl (not the transcript — reasoning-effort is a request-time setting the transcript never records), buckets dispatches by their data.effort tag, prices at the run's dominant model (ESTIMATE — events carry no model) and reports coverage_pct vs the top-line. --selftest runs the table
