  review-progress <read|write> <run-dir> <issue> [--phase1-pass --diff-hash H | --phase2 STATUS [--findings PATH] [--attempts N] | --outage-retry]   FAFF-329: per-issue review checkpoint at \`<run-dir>/<issue>/review-progress.json\` so a re-dispatched build subagent RESUMES the graft review step (skips a completed Phase-1/Phase-2) instead of repeating it. read → ReviewProgress JSON (exit 0) / exit 3 if absent (no checkpoint yet, not an error); write --phase1-pass --diff-hash records the passing Phase-1 verdict + the diff hash it was computed against (the diff-identity guard — a resume skips Phase-1 only if the CURRENT diff still matches); write --phase2 <pending|in_flight|complete|skipped_deadline|skipped_unreachable> records Phase-2 progress; write --outage-retry (FAFF-403) increments the top-level outage_retries counter (absent → 1, requires an existing record — exit 2 if none) for graft's retry-later hold on a mandatory-review \`unavailable\` verdict. PURE JSON (no tracker/network); a HINT never authoritative over git/PR truth; exit 2 usage/bad-status; --selftest runs the fold table
  build-progress <read|write> <run-dir> <issue> [--build-complete --diff-hash H --branch B]   FAFF-402: per-issue build-complete checkpoint at \`<run-dir>/<issue>/build-progress.json\` — written at graft build-complete (Step 8b) AFTER the branch is pushed to origin, so a re-dispatched graft RESUMES at review (recreating the worktree from origin/<branch>, skipping the build) instead of rebuilding. read → BuildProgress JSON (exit 0) / exit 3 if absent (no checkpoint yet, not an error); write --build-complete --diff-hash --branch records the remote-three-dot diff hash it was gated at + the pushed branch (the diff-identity guard — a resume skips the build only if the CURRENT remote diff still matches). PURE JSON (no tracker/network/git — the diff hash is computed in graft prose); a HINT never authoritative over git truth; exit 2 usage/missing-flag; --selftest runs the fold table
  effects <declare|observe|check> --run <run-id> [--issue ID] [--step NAME] [--ts ISO] [--json] [--root DIR]   FAFF-106: escaped-side-effect detection via a declared-effects ledger — the PRODUCER of the escaped-side-effect signal Sentry (FAFF-49) consumes. declare/observe read an EffectDescriptor {kind ∈ closed EFFECT_KINDS, target, reversible?} (object or array) on stdin and append a LedgerEntry (CLI fills schema/run_id/seq/ts envelope; kind_of_entry/issue/step required) to .faff/runs/<run-id>/declared-effects.jsonl — a PARALLEL ledger, never an events.jsonl schema bump; exit 0 ok / 1 bad descriptor (unknown kind / missing target) / 2 malformed JSON or missing --run/--issue/--step / 3 run-dir missing. check computes observed-MINUS-declared per (issue, step) using exact-target + "*" matching and emits {escapes:[EscapeSignal{signal:"escaped-side-effect",issue,step,escaped[],event_seq}], any_escape} (--json); a missing ledger file is a clean state ({escapes:[],any_escape:false}, exit 0 — NOT exit 3). Detection only — never aborts (Sentry/FAFF-37's job); FAFF-352: the orchestrator bridges any_escape into Sentry via \`faff sentry check\`'s \`--forbidden-side-effect\` CLI flag (the signals.forbidden_side_effect seam's CLI surface), run immediately after this check at every between-units checkpoint. PURE (no tracker/network, writes only under the run dir); --selftest runs the descriptor/matching/escape table
  sentry <check|abort> [--run-dir DIR] [--forbidden-side-effect] [--budget-json JSON] [--member-beats-json JSON] [--authority available|channel-D-only] [--now-ms MS | --now ISO] [--issue ID] [--signal NAME] [--worktree PATH] [--json] [--root DIR]   FAFF-49: live-run derailment detection + hard kill-switch (the L4 supervisory lane). check READS a live run's append-only surface (events.jsonl + run-ledger.json + the effective heartbeat — the dedicated heartbeat file overlaid over the legacy owner.last_heartbeat field, FAFF-355 — + a CONSUMED \`faff budget check\` child call) WITHOUT mutating it, and emits DerailmentVerdicts {signal,severity,evidence} + the chosen intervention (continue|pause|correct|abort); wall-clock-runaway evidence names heartbeat_source ("heartbeat-file" | "owner.last_heartbeat") — never a hardcoded field name; exit 0 (report-only). FAFF-326 (Sentry-2, Channel A): \`correct\` sits between pause and abort and is reachable ONLY when authority is available — derived from a CHILD call to \`corrective-integrity --consumer corrective\` (never a direct require, keeping this a pure governance span; region direction, ADR 0042), fail-safe to "channel-D-only" on any non-OK child; only fix-review-thrash's mapped pause upgrades, every abort route is unchanged. --authority is a HERMETIC test-only override seam (explicit-flag-only, mirrors --budget-json/--now-ms) — production never passes it. FAFF-352: --forbidden-side-effect (boolean, check only) sets signals.forbidden_side_effect — the orchestrator passes it IFF \`faff effects check\` reported any_escape at this checkpoint — arming the forbidden-side-effect-attempt trip (severity trip → intervention abort); absent, the signal degrades to no-signal exactly as before. --now-ms <epoch-ms> / --now <ISO> is a HERMETIC test/diagnostic-only clock override for the time-based wall-clock signal — explicit flag only (no ambient/env form), precedence --now-ms > --now > Date.now() (the production default; no production caller passes it); an unparseable injected value exits 2 (never a silent fall-through). FAFF-425: check's OWN inability to read the run's ledger (explicitly-named and absent, or present-but-corrupt) — or a budget consult that hit the same fault reading its ledger — is a distinct own-fault, never folded into "no derailment": {indeterminate:true,reason,verdicts:[],intervention:"continue",tripped:false}, exit 3; a legitimately empty surface (no run requested, none found) is unaffected, unchanged all-clear at exit 0. abort leaves RESUMABLE state — commits in-flight --worktree WIP to its branch (park-protocol shape, never force-reset), marks the ledger aborted-resumable; exit 0 / 2 malformed ledger / 3 no run dir. PURE evaluator (reads only the orchestrator surface — un-subvertable by construction); --selftest runs the table. FAFF-327 (fleet / member-resolved supervision): auto-detected — in-flight members (a build-start event with no terminal ledger outcome) are derived from the same events+ledger surface, and each in-flight member's OWN heartbeat.<issue> file (written by \`faff heartbeat --unit\`) is read to resolve its liveness. A stalled member emits a wall-clock-runaway verdict carrying scope:"member" + member:<issue>, capped at intervention "pause" — it NEVER escalates to run-wide "abort" by itself; ALL members stalled still trips the RUN-scoped wall-clock-runaway (unchanged) once the run heartbeat file itself goes stale, preserving the existing kill-switch. fix-review-thrash / repeated-identical-failure verdicts additionally gain the same scope/member fields when their evidence names a single issue (additive attribution only — their own mapped intervention is unchanged). A run with no in-flight members is byte-equivalent to the pre-327 payload. \`sentry check\` performs no writes on any fleet path. --member-beats-json is a HERMETIC test-only override (mirrors --budget-json) for the member-heartbeat read; production always reads real heartbeat.<issue> files.
  sentry-poller <start|stop|status|run> [--run-dir DIR] [--interval-secs N] [--json] [--root DIR]   FAFF-470: ADR-0065's PRIMARY watchdog locus — a mint-scoped DETACHED, unref'd child process that loops the unmodified \`sentry check\`/\`sentry abort\` CLI on a fixed interval (default 90s) so a wall-clock-runaway orchestrator that stops reaching checkpoints is still caught from OUTSIDE its control flow. Carries no detection math of its own — every verdict originates from a \`sentry check\` child call; its only ledger-writing action is the existing \`sentry abort\` child (ledger-mark only, never a process signal). start: idempotent on a live pid, clears a stale stop sentinel, spawns detached+unref'd, writes sentry-poller.json {pid,started_at,interval_secs} atomically; exit 3 no run dir/ledger, 2 bad --interval-secs. stop: writes the sentry-poller.stop sentinel (race-free — no kill signal is ever sent), exit 0 always once a run dir resolves. status: {running,pid,started_at,interval_secs} from the handle + a kill(pid,0) liveness probe. run: the internal foreground loop (spawned by start; prose never calls it) — self-stops on the sentinel, a gone run dir, or owner.status leaving "running"; on L4 (\`level:"L4"\`) + tripped abort, runs \`sentry abort\` and appends one sentry-checkpoint event; a non-L4 trip only logs advisory-trip (mint-scoped acting, unforked consult); a \`sentry check\` fault (exit 3/unparseable) logs indeterminate and keeps polling, capped at 20 consecutive faults (fault-cap-exit) to bound orphan-process risk. All tick telemetry goes to sentry-poller.log (best-effort append). --selftest drives the pure tick-decision core over the full dispatch table.
  audit <run-id> [--root DIR] [--issue ISSUE] [--json]   FAFF-289: read-only run-reconstruction forensics view — join the three substrates a finished run leaves on disk (events.jsonl timeline + run-ledger.json final state + .faff/provenance/<ISSUE>.json intake proofs) into one who/what/why reconstruction: per-run lifecycle (started/ended/duration/complete/phases/owner), one rollup per admitted-or-evented issue (provenance via/initiated + its events in seq order + ledger outcome + park cause), a budget summary (ledger envelope + tokens_at_start + budget-checkpoint events — NEVER live recompute), a FAFF-352 supervision summary (sentry-checkpoint events in seq order + last_intervention — proof a \`faff sentry check\` consult ran at every between-units checkpoint), and a coherence block (reuses auditLedger for undispatched/invalid + adds events<->ledger mismatches + missing substrates + FAFF-354's containment recompute: containment_mismatches — every recorded containment-check event re-walked with the SAME parseAncestry/subtreeContains pipeline, a disagreement or unparseable ancestry_raw ("unreproducible") listed as {seq,issue,recorded,recomputed}; unrecorded_creates — ledger.discovered_scope_filed > 0 with zero containment-check events; both flip coherence.clean false — DETECTIVE, never preventive). PURE (no tracker/network/LLM); degrade-don't-crash (reconstructs from whatever exists, reports gaps); coherence is REPORTED never gated (a readable run exits 0 even when incoherent). exit 0 readable / 2 no run-id / 3 no run dir, both core files missing, or --issue not in run. --json emits the Reconstruction object; --selftest runs the join table
  lights-out [--check] [--until HH:MM] [--max N] [--slot-unreachable review|spec_review ...] [--id RUN-ID] [--resume RUN-ID] [--json] [--root DIR]   FAFF-225: the L4 lights-out entry point / runner. FAFF-527: --resume RUN-ID re-enters an EXISTING run's ledger under a fresh session instead of minting a new run — reconstructs each admitted issue's true position from the ledger + per-issue artifacts + forge ground truth (reconcile-proven merges skip and never re-merge; ledger-vs-forge divergences park needs-human while the rest resumes; checkpoint-less in-flight issues coarse-rebuild), re-fires the full mint preflight against current config, closes the prior budget session into budget.sessions[] and re-baselines (never undercounts), and continues the SAME run_id/ledger/events seq stream (owner_history + abort_history + resume[] + owner.epoch fence, never a second run-start). Re-enterable iff aborted-resumable / escalate-class stop_reason / stale-heartbeat dead-running; live-running + done-clean + unparseable-ledger exit 2 untouched; --resume+--id exit 2; --resume --check reconstructs + prints the ResumePlan side-effect-free — "leave the building" as one enforced action. Runs a fail-closed BASIC preflight over v1's launch preconditions (container-check contained — WARN→BLOCK on this path only; review + spec_review slots reachable, unreachable==absent; a budget ceiling set — FAFF-427: budget.cost is the recommended default (priced per-model x per-class from a built-in map, unconditionally), or budget.tokens/budget.until; FAFF-446: a config still setting the removed budget.price_per_mtok REFUSES on its own gate budget-price-per-mtok-removed naming the raw value; a malformed budget.until/--until (not valid HH:MM) REFUSES on its own gate budget-until-invalid naming the raw value — regardless of any other ceiling set, since a run must never mint a ledger carrying malformed until (FAFF-364); when malformed until is the ONLY ceiling, budget-ceiling ALSO fires alongside it; all