  backends <resolve|realizable> --refs a,b,c [--requires local] [--harness NAME] [--json] [--root DIR]   FAFF-523: the shared named model/provider/auth backend config namespace — a top-level backends: map (name -> {provider,model,host,auth,api_key_env?,egress,reasoning_off?,timeout?}) generalizing engines: (folds in at load, name collision = hard error), referenced by an ordered refs: list (index 0 first-served, no "primary"). auth (subscription-seat|api-key|none) and egress (local|external) are explicit-preferred, else derived (api_key_env present -> api-key; keyless anthropic -> subscription-seat, binding to the ambient interactive session with no seat_ref handle; loopback/RFC1918/tailscale host -> local egress, else external). 'resolve' prints the resolved chain as JSON (fail-loud exit 2 on an unknown name or a namespace merge error). 'realizable' runs the run-start fail-closed check: any requires:local ref that resolves egress:external refuses with a residency-violation naming it; a whole chain with zero (harness,provider,auth)-admitted, host-set refs refuses chain-unrealizable (v1 pins harness to the single value the CLI passes today — the harness-varying half of the matrix lands with FAFF-395's faff run spine); exit 0 realizable / 1 refused. --selftest runs the derive/merge/resolve/realizable/config-check-guard table
`;


